      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1752168811306,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Q: If you have 3 apples and get 2 more, how many apples do you have?\nA:\n1. Start with 3 apples.\n2. Add 2 more: 3 + 2 = 5.\nAnswer: 5\n\nQ: John has 4 books and buys 3 more. How many books does he have?\nA:\n1. John starts with 4 books.\n2. He buys 3 more: 4 + 3 = 7.\nAnswer: 7\n\nQ: A box contains 6 red balls and someone adds 5 blue balls. How many balls are in the box now?\nA:\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Q: If you have 3 apples and get 2 more, how many apples do you have?\nA:\n1. Start with 3 apples.\n2. Add 2 more: 3 + 2 = 5.\nAnswer: 5\n\nQ: John has 4 books and buys 3 more. How many books does he have?\nA:\n1. John starts with 4 books.\n2. He buys 3 more: 4 + 3 = 7.\nAnswer: 7\n\nQ: A box contains 6 red balls and someone adds 5 blue balls. How many balls are in the box now?\nA:\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
